# ============================================================
# .GITIGNORE — Insurance Premium Prediction ML System
# Rebuilt for: GitHub push + Render (API) + Streamlit Cloud (dashboard)
#
# RULE OF THUMB: anything Render or Streamlit Cloud reads at runtime
# MUST be pushed to GitHub — these platforms deploy directly from your
# repo, they don't see your local machine's files.
#
# MUST be pushed (do NOT ignore):
#   premium_models/     -> champion .joblib + latest_model.json + model
#                           cards + monitor_scores.csv + feature_drift_report.csv
#                           + challenger_log.json  (Render loads the model from
#                           here; Streamlit reads the CSV/JSON files from here)
#   data/                -> sample dataset (small file — see note below)
#   src/ serving/ services/ monitoring/ simulation/ scripts/  -> all source code
#   requirements*.txt, Dockerfile*, render.yaml, docker-compose.yml
#   docs/                -> README images/gifs/svg (renders on GitHub)
#   notebooks/           -> EDA notebook + html export
# ============================================================

# ── Python cache/build artifacts ─────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# ── Virtual environments / secrets ───────────────────────────
venv/
env/
.env
.venv/

# ── Jupyter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── MLflow tracking store — large, regenerable locally, not needed
#    for Render/Streamlit (they only read premium_models/, not mlruns/) ─
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
mlflow.db

# ── Prediction logs — auto-generated at runtime by the API, not
#    needed for the app to boot; keep the folder with a placeholder
#    so git tracks it, but not the growing CSV itself ─────────
!logs/*.csv
logs/*.log
!logs/.gitkeep

# ── Test / coverage artifacts ─────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# ── OS / editor junk ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ============================================================
# ⚠️ SAFETY NET — do NOT commit the FULL real Kaggle competition
# file (train.csv, ~185MB) if you ever copy it into data/ — GitHub
# hard-blocks any single file over 100MB. Only the small sample
# dataset should live in data/. If your real train.csv ever ends
# up inside this repo folder, uncomment the line below (rename to
# match your actual filename) before committing:
# data/train.csv
# ============================================================